matter|issue|NOUN|subject needing attention|A subject, situation, or problem that people consider or discuss.|vấn đề; sự việc|We agreed to discuss the matter after everyone had read the letter.|Chúng tôi thống nhất sẽ bàn về vấn đề này sau khi mọi người đọc thư.|Countable in this sense; a matter for discussion names a particular issue.|0
matter|be-important|VERB|have importance|To be important or make a difference to someone or something.|quan trọng; có ý nghĩa|Your choice of words matters when you apologize.|Cách bạn chọn từ ngữ rất quan trọng khi xin lỗi.|Intransitive; matter to someone identifies the person who regards something as important.|1
matter|physical-substance|NOUN|substance with physical existence|The physical substance of which things are made.|vật chất|The class examined tiny particles of matter through a microscope.|Lớp học quan sát những hạt vật chất nhỏ qua kính hiển vi.|Uncountable in this sense; not the countable matter meaning a topic for discussion.|2
overcrowded|too-full|ADJECTIVE|holding too many people or things|Containing more people or things than the available space can comfortably hold.|quá đông; chật chội do quá tải|The waiting room became overcrowded after the morning buses arrived.|Phòng chờ trở nên quá đông sau khi các chuyến xe buýt buổi sáng đến.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; overcrowded with names what fills the space.|-
so-called|named-with-distance|ADJECTIVE|described by a particular name|Described by a particular name, often with doubt about whether that name is suitable.|được gọi là; cái gọi là|The so-called quiet carriage was full of loud conversations.|Toa tàu được gọi là yên tĩnh lại đầy những cuộc nói chuyện ồn ào.|Usually before a noun; can report a label neutrally or suggest doubt, depending on context.|0
weight|heaviness|NOUN|how heavy something is|The amount of heaviness that a person or thing has.|trọng lượng; cân nặng|The parcel's weight was greater than the label suggested.|Trọng lượng của bưu kiện lớn hơn mức ghi trên nhãn.|Usually uncountable for heaviness; the weight of something names the measured property.|0
author|writer|NOUN|person who writes a work|A person who writes a book, article, or other written work.|tác giả|The author answered questions about the ending of her novel.|Tác giả trả lời các câu hỏi về phần kết tiểu thuyết của mình.|Countable; author of a work identifies what the person wrote.|0
